#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
replicate_networking.py

Purpose
-------
Replicate (PROD -> DR):
- Security Groups (create missing, then sync inbound/outbound rules; no duplicates)
- Target Groups
- Load Balancers + Listeners + Listener Rules

Key guarantees
--------------
- PROD is READ-ONLY: this script never calls create/modify/delete in PROD sessions.
- DR is CREATE/MODIFY as needed (idempotent-ish): does not recreate existing resources;
  instead it reconciles and adds missing pieces.
- Two-pass SG sync: prevents SG->SG referenced rules from being skipped.
- Tags: does NOT copy tags (and specifically never attempts to set aws:* tags).
- Stack-suffix SG names: if a PROD SG name ends with a random/stack suffix (e.g. "-wf6YhVwT12IE"),
  DR name will be the same base + a deterministic DR suffix (NO "-dr-").
  If DR already has the same base with some other suffix, we adopt that instead of creating a new one.

Config
------
JSON file, example:

{
  "prod_profile": "prod-sso",
  "dr_profile": "default",
  "prod_region": "us-west-2",
  "dr_region": "us-east-1",

  "vpc_map": {
    "prod_vpc_id": "vpc-0236....",
    "dr_vpc_id": "vpc-011a....",
    "subnet_map": {
      "subnet-prod-1": "subnet-dr-1",
      "subnet-prod-2": "subnet-dr-2"
    }
  },

  "filters": {
    "security_group_name_prefixes": [],
    "load_balancer_name_prefixes": [],
    "target_group_name_prefixes": []
  },

  "cert_map": {
    "arn:aws:acm:us-west-2:PROD:certificate/xxxx": "arn:aws:acm:us-east-1:DR:certificate/yyyy"
  }
}

Notes
-----
- cert_map is OPTIONAL. If missing (or empty), listeners that require certificates are skipped.
- Subnet mapping is required to create LBs.
"""

